course: dictionary
lesson: 2244
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word craft is one of them. To find the right meaning, read the words around it, because they are its context. «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts» means making things by hand, since you collect things to paint, glue and make into something.
explain: «The submersible (a small deep-diving craft) Trieste» uses craft to mean a vehicle. The brackets give you a clue: a deep-diving craft is a machine that travels. You may already know this meaning from words like aircraft and spacecraft.
explain: Always check by swapping in your meaning. Would «a small boat» fit in «a small craft»? Yes, so craft means a boat here. Would «making by hand» fit in «craft knives»? The knives are used for crafts, so the meaning fits. When the meaning fits the sentence, you have found the right one.
fact: Craft can be a noun or a verb. As a verb, «to craft» means to make something carefully and skilfully.
fact: As a noun, craft means an activity where you make things by hand, like painting, sewing, cutting and gluing.
fact: A craft can also be a boat, ship, plane or spacecraft: «a small craft».
fact: Craft can also mean a skill or job that needs skilful hands, like woodwork or pottery.
fact: Craft knives are for grown-ups only, because their blades are very sharp and slip easily.
exercise: «Collect conkers, acorns and pine cones for crafts, but never eat them.» In this sentence, what does crafts mean? | Tricks used to fool people | Sailing across the sea | Being very tall | *Making things by hand, like gluing and painting
exercise: In «the submersible (a small deep-diving craft) Trieste», what kind of thing is a craft? | *A vehicle, such as a boat or submarine | A kind of paint | Something you can eat
exercise: «Running with scissors or a craft knife can turn a small trip into a deep stab wound.» What does the sentence warn you not to do? | *Run with scissors or a craft knife | Open a parcel carefully | Share conkers with friends | Make a craft table
test: «Ella wanted to craft a card for Mum, so she carefully cut and glued the paper.» What does craft mean here? | To sing loudly | To trick people with clever words | *To make something carefully and skilfully | To sail across the sea
test: «The small craft sailed into the harbour.» What kind of craft is this? | *A boat | A kind of glue | An old trick
exam: Tom says craft always means making things by hand. Which sentence shows he is wrong? | «Paint and glue are used in craft lessons.» | «Craft fairs sell handmade things.» | *«The hovercraft zoomed across the river.» | «She crafted a clay pot.»
